Error [jet.AppFeatureNotOnTarget]: App feature `.csr` needs target `JS`, but the resolved target is `Wasm`.
  --> tests/ui/app_capability_target.jet:4:23
    |
  4 | run: fn() { web.app().csr().serve() }
    |                       ^^^
 Why: App is one type across targets, but each feature must be supported by the target selected by `#Target` or the package manifest; rejecting it in sema keeps native and web codegen on one meaning. During `jet check`, Jet reports this diagnostic.
 Fix: Choose a build target that supports `.csr` (for example `#Target(JS)` for browser features or a native target for server features), or remove that feature.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E-APP-TARGET-FEATURE
